Fury Remastered @VERSION@ (@COMMIT@) - @PLATFORM@
==================================================

An unofficial, fan-made desktop port of ATV Offroad Fury 2 (USA v2.00), written
in Rust. It is not affiliated with, authorized or endorsed by the game's
publishers or developers. The original game's resources that this port needs to
run are packed into this download; you do not need the disc, an emulator or
anything else installed. The packed resources remain the property of their
owners. The software is provided as is, without warranty.

This is an early build. It runs the same Rust engine as the web version at
https://furyremastered.com/ (which switched to it on 2026-10-23): the title screen
and menus, the 40 original venues, the ATVs, motorcycles and riders, Freeride and
races against the original CPU riders, online multiplayer, the HUD and minimap,
audio and settings (including key and controller remapping). It is not finished;
progress and known gaps are in the dev log at https://furyremastered.com/devlog.html.

How to run
----------
@RUN@

Controls: drive with W/A/S/D or the arrow keys or a gamepad (the same defaults as
the web version, remappable in Pause > Settings > Controls); R or Backspace resets,
C changes the camera, Z/X orbit, H shows the keyboard card, Esc or P pauses. With --free you get a free camera instead (W/A/S/D move, Q/E down/up, hold
Shift to go faster, drag with the mouse to look around).

Command line (optional): --venue ID (skip the menus), --quad 1-46, --rider 0|1,
--race [--laps N --cpu 0|3|4 --difficulty 1|2], --graphics original|enhanced|high,
--crash original|crazy|gorn, --free, --camera x,y,z,yaw,pitch,focal,
--capture out.png 1280x720 (render one frame to a PNG and exit), --verify-content
(check the packed content and exit), --version.
--content DIR or --pack FILE use an external content source instead of the
packed one.
@NOTES@
Project: https://github.com/nrgapple/atv-offroad-fury-2-web

The soundtrack is decoded with Symphonia (https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia),
used unmodified under the Mozilla Public License 2.0
(https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/); its source code is available there and on crates.io.
